# Example .npmrc — install this package from GitHub Packages
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR
#   npm needs to know that packages under the @vishalsharma7nov scope come from
#   GitHub Packages (npm.pkg.github.com), not from the public npmjs.com registry.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file into your app root as `.npmrc`
#   2. Create a GitHub personal access token with `read:packages`
#   3. Put the token in your environment as GITHUB_TOKEN, or paste it in place
#      of ${GITHUB_TOKEN} below (do not commit real tokens to git)
#
# ALTERNATIVE (no GitHub Packages)
#   npm install github:vishalsharma7nov/react-native-proto#v0.1.0
#
@vishalsharma7nov:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
